%I A094224 #45 Sep 09 2026 22:31:28
%S A094224 1,18,28,6,6,58,22,13,44
%N A094224 Number of digits in the least n-parasitic number.
%C A094224 A k-parasitic number, where 1<=k<=9, is one which is equal to k times the number whose digits are a cyclic permutation of its leftmost digit to the right.
%D A094224 P. Tougne, "Jeux Mathématiques", Prob. 8, pp. 104 and 107 Aug. 1982 issue of Pour La Science (French edition of 'Scientific American'), Paris.
%H A094224 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parasitic_number">Parasitic number</a>.
%F A094224 a(n) = min_{k=n..9} (order of 10 mod (10n-1)/gcd(k, 10n-1)). - _Robert D. Rosales_, Aug 11 2026
%F A094224 a(n) = A055642(A092697(n)). - _Michel Marcus_, Aug 15 2026
%e A094224 We have the a(4)=6-digit 4-transposable number 410256=4*102564, and the a(5)=6-digit 5-transposable number 714285=5*142857.
%t A094224 Table[Min[If[# == 1, 1, MultiplicativeOrder[10, #]] & /@ ((10 n - 1)/GCD[Range[n, 9], 10 n - 1])], {n, 1, 9}] (* _Robert D. Rosales_, Aug 11 2026 *)
%o A094224 (Python)
%o A094224 from sympy import n_order; from math import gcd
%o A094224 print([min(n_order(10, m) if (m := (10*n - 1) // gcd(k, 10*n - 1)) > 1 else 1 for k in range(n, 10)) for n in range(1, 10)]) # _Robert D. Rosales_, Aug 11 2026
%Y A094224 Cf. A092697 (value of the least n-parasitic number).
%K A094224 fini,full,nonn,base,changed
%O A094224 1,2
